                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "YHgv2",
                  "name": "Contract",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A lettermark in the interface face, not artwork: the display weight at −2% tracking on a pine tile. The name is an initialism — where is my money? — so the lock-up ends in the question mark it stands for, set in the accent blue that carries every other query in the product: links, selection, focus. The question mark never appears alone and never on the tile, because a lone ? in a rounded square is a help affordance in every other interface and would be read as one here. It identifies the product and nothing else — never a link to a marketing page, never a home button competing with Overview, never coloured by state. The mark alone is what the rail uses; the lock-up is what the labelled sidebar uses. Pine is a fill here, which is the only way the brand green may appear beside an income amount in dark theme.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": "$type-size-body-sm",
