                  "name": "Contract",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Three states per row so each specimen keeps a realistic width. The rest border uses color-control-border, a token separate from decorative dividers, because a control's boundary is information needed to identify it: it measures 3.7:1 in light and 3.5:1 in dark against the field's own fill, and clears 3:1 against the canvas and the disabled fill too. Placeholder text uses color-text-placeholder at 6.2:1 — a placeholder is live content, not an inactive control, so the contrast exemption does not cover it. The value never wraps; the field clips and scrolls. Affixes, the error message and the label live outside this atom.",
