            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "cGAD8",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$color-text-primary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Molecules",
              "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
              "fontSize": 32,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.6
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "c2TIc",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Small compositions of atoms with one job each. Variants are rows, states are columns, same as the atoms — and anything a molecule owns, its atoms deliberately do not.",
              "lineHeight": 1.55,
              "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "x7TE5Q",
          "name": "Form field",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "e5srUU",
              "name": "Spec header",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Gc17K",
                  "name": "Name",
                  "fill": "$color-text-primary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Form field",
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": "$type-size-heading-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "e3i8ee",
                  "name": "Contract",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Label, control, and exactly one message. The message row reserves two lines and is always present — a hint at rest, an error when invalid — so validation never moves the content beneath it. Reserving one line would not be enough: the moment a message wraps, every field below it shifts, which is what a no-reflow promise has to survive.\n\nTwo lines is a reservation, not a clip. An error longer than two lines grows the row and does move the content below, and that is the correct trade: a clipped error is unperceivable, and SC 3.3.1 requires the error be identified in text. Treat the growth as the signal it is — a message that does not fit is a message that is explaining rather than instructing. Name the fix and stop.\n\nThe label is always visible: a placeholder is not a label, because it disappears the moment someone starts typing. The error carries an icon and is announced in code, so it never depends on the red alone. The focus ring lives on a wrapper rather than the control, so focus costs no layout shift either. Amount fields hold an unsigned magnitude; direction is a separate control, never a typed minus.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": "$type-size-body-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
