                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The page's own title bar, not the product's. It names where you are, holds the one action this page is for, and nothing else — a header that accumulates buttons is a page that has not decided what it is for. Breadcrumbs sit above the title when the page has ancestors; tabs sit below it when the page has peer views.",
