                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "uhE4s",
                  "name": "Contract",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Three regions, top to bottom: the brand, the destinations, and a footer pinned to the bottom by a spacer so it sits at the foot whatever the viewport height. The footer holds the account trigger and the collapse control. Top-level destinations, grouped but never nested — one level of depth, because the rail has nowhere to render a second. Rows are Nav item instances, so a sidebar row, a menu row and a sub-nav row are identical by construction rather than by care. Section headers degrade to dividers in the rail; child items would degrade to nothing, which is why there are none. The brand degrades to its mark, the account trigger to its avatar, and the collapse control reverses its glyph; nothing disappears between the two forms, which is what makes the rail a rendering of this component rather than a second one. Width sets which form appears by default — rail below 1200 CSS px — and the control overrides that for the session. Below 768 there is no sidebar to collapse, so the control is not rendered rather than shown disabled.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$type-family-body",
                  "fontSize": "$type-size-body-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
