                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "CC09p",
                  "name": "Contract",
                  "fill": "$color-text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Header, rows, and the bar that reports what you are looking at. The header is sticky and its sort state is programmatically identifiable, not just an arrow. Selection is a row property, and the header checkbox is indeterminate whenever the page is partly selected — never silently 'all'. The count is always visible because people reconcile against it. Zebra striping is a second channel behind the row border, so a table still parses with striping turned off.",
